---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { BAND } from "../data/band";

// Update this whenever the policy's wording changes.
const LAST_UPDATED = "30 September 2026";
---

<Layout
  title={`Cookie policy | ${BAND.name}`}
  description={`How ${BAND.name}'s website uses cookies: in short, it doesn't.`}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-6 pt-16 pb-20 text-body [&_a]:underline [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_h2]:font-display [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-ink [&_p]:mb-4 [&_p]:leading-relaxed">
    <h1 class="m-0 mb-2 font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-ink sm:text-5xl">Cookie policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

    <p class="text-lg text-ink">
      <strong>The short version: this website doesn't use cookies.</strong> There's no analytics,
      advertising or tracking, and we don't store anything in your browser. Our fonts are served
      from our own site, and blog images come from our content system, Sanity, which doesn't set
      cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>YouTube videos</h2>
    <p>
      Some posts include videos. Nothing is loaded from YouTube until you press play. When you do,
      the video plays from YouTube in its privacy-enhanced mode, and YouTube may then set cookies or
      store data in your browser, as described in{" "}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>. If
      you'd rather it didn't, just don't press play.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Our hosting provider, Cloudflare, may set a strictly necessary cookie to protect the site from
      abuse. It isn't used to track you.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      We link to our Instagram, Facebook and YouTube pages. Those sites have their own cookie
      policies, which apply once you visit them.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email us at <a href={`mailto:${BAND.email}`}>{BAND.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
